      "writtenOn": "2024-12-11T18:02:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You hinted in our offline talks that the switch statement wasn\u0027t causing too much of a performance hit here. If we needed to, I would imagine that specializations along the lines of:\n - srgb + srgb\n - pq -\u003e pq\n - hlginv -\u003e hlg\n - srgb -\u003e pq\n - pq -\u003e srgb\n - srgb -\u003e hlg\n - hlginv -\u003e srgb\n \nwould be reasonable, with the most commonly used one being srgb-\u003esrgb.  Were you able to measure with images that had to undergo these colorspace conversions, or was a lot of it being avoided by hitting the `sk_premul_alpha` specialization or the `flags \u003d\u003d 0` specialization?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 60,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 60,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "cae0cb54c32e7dfc42a0de5d5a9e4319ac11f67b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dce7d68b_8845f241",
        "filename": "src/sksl/sksl_graphite_frag.sksl",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 96,
