        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-12-11T18:02:45Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "When Jim added this optimization, I know we saw that it was very effective on the M GPU family, but we haven\u0027t measured how well it works for Android and Windows devices.\n\nIn particular, a lot of Chrome image decoding logic exists to do a one-time conversion of the image into the target colorspace so that it doesn\u0027t have to be applied each time it\u0027s re-rendered. Similarly, all the internal image filter surfaces and layer surfaces have a high chance of being the same color space and color type as the input image.  If this flags check isn\u0027t giving us as much benefit on other devices, we should consider doing an identity variation that doesn\u0027t add the colorspace transform block.\n\nThis is an independent thought from the benefits you\u0027ve already got here.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 96,
        "startChar": 7,
        "endLine": 96,
        "endChar": 19
      },
      "revId": "cae0cb54c32e7dfc42a0de5d5a9e4319ac11f67b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
